00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:03.120
Okay so, one of the things
that's really important

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.190
when you are thinking

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.820
about creating physical
activity experiences

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:11.750
for your children, are that you want

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:15.240
to accumulate about 60 minutes
of daily physical activity

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:19.560
for school aged children
around ages six to 17 years old

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:22.760
and this is recommendations
that come from CDC

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.400
and for preschool aged children,

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.200
thinking about three to five years old,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.190
there isn't a set time,
but just making sure

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:33.720
that there's getting physical
activity throughout the day.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.093
So, some specific examples
of the kinds of things

00:04:36.093 --> 00:04:38.705
that you can do with your younger children

00:04:38.705 --> 00:04:41.110
are using things around your house.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.780
It doesn't have to be
elaborate, doesn't have

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.020
to even take a lot of time as
long as you're just providing

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:49.510
that opportunity for your
children to move and one example

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:53.330
is using things like paper
plates or if you have pillows

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:56.930
or even a hand towel something
flat and you can spread

00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:00.750
that around an area and have
them jump from rock to rock.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:04.710
And so this works on the skills
of balance and local motor

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:07.410
and leaping and then if
you're able to go outside,

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.120
you could use sidewalk chalk

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.300
and draw circles and have them leaping.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.220
Really, at the early childhood age

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:17.340
around three to five, imaginative movement

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:20.520
is really good for young children.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.610
Having them move their
bodies in different ways,

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:25.437
so asking them, "can you
make your body like a circle,

00:05:25.437 --> 00:05:28.870
"can you make your body like
a triangle or the letter S?"

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.430
And so getting them to be creative

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.590
while they're moving their body

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:34.770
and exploring how their body
moves in different ways.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:38.620
I know we probably, the
go to exercise of movement

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:42.380
is walking, and it's really
good even for little ones

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.790
but specifically for little ones having

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:48.010
to practice those local
motor movements again

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:51.800
as well as galloping and
skipping and hopping,

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.210
they can do that along the sidewalk.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.520
So, just thinking about ways

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.680
that they can move while walking.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.370
In your house or even outside you

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.407
can ask them, "touch three
things that are green,

00:06:02.407 --> 00:06:05.347
"touch one thing that is
red," so just having them,

00:06:05.347 --> 00:06:09.020
you're working on colors and
then following directions

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:11.790
and they're moving at the same
time, so very simple things

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:16.790
and then of course, one that
is easy to do, is with music

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:19.020
and using music as a great tool.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:22.340
So, playing different types
of music with fast tempos

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.667
or slower tempos and asking them,

00:06:24.667 --> 00:06:27.810
"well how can you move your
body to the beat of this song?"

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:30.590
So, if they're moving fast,
they can get kind of upbeat

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.220
or if they're slow,

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:35.300
and they move their body
slow, classical music

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.740
is a great opportunity to use

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:39.130
because the variations in the tempo

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:43.200
or if there's loud drums
or clashing symbols.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.750
And so, we have a lot of
resources at shapeamerica.org,

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:51.400
especially on our early
childhood calendars

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.480
are really great.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.930
We have tons of resources
there with plethora of ideas

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.653
for our little, our young
friends, our young children.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.694
So, specifically going back
to school aged children,

00:07:02.694 --> 00:07:06.450
that's categorized as six
to 17 year old children.

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.730
And so, really making sure
they get an hour of moderate

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:12.500
to vigorous physical
activity throughout the day.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:13.950
So, that means their heart rate is up,

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:14.810
they're breathing harder

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:17.543
and if they did it long
enough, they get sweaty.

