00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:47.583
- Absolutely.

00:07:47.583 --> 00:07:51.460
So, you don't need a
lot of space necessarily

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.300
but this is where creativity comes

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.702
in really great, so one
thing that, using the things

00:07:55.702 --> 00:07:57.420
that you already have in your house.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:00.420
So, one example is if you have Candyland

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.070
or another card game or Monopoly

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:06.100
or something like that you can
use the cards from that game,

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:08.720
and assign exercises to the colors

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:10.630
or the suits or the character.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.010
And then, so for example, in Candyland

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:16.930
if you draw a blue
color, you can do running

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.270
in place for 20 seconds
or something like that.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:20.630
And one thing you'll hear me talk

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:23.790
about a lot through this
is allowing your children

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:25.830
to have choice, that's really important

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:26.927
so, ask them, "what do you want,

00:08:26.927 --> 00:08:28.857
"what should we do if we pick blue?"

00:08:28.857 --> 00:08:30.170
"What should we do if we pick red?"

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:31.270
So, getting them involved

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:34.850
and coming up with the rules of the game.

