00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.890
But that's interesting.
- Oh, I'm down with it.

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:04.930
- It's kind of a little more
rigorous, a walk is nice

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:08.820
but if you can maybe work
up a sweat, dancing, yoga,

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:12.160
running, some type of,
you know, shooting hoops,

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:14.200
you know, socially distance
just with your family,

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:15.865
I guess, stuff like that.

00:10:15.865 --> 00:10:19.990
- Yeah so, walking is a
great is a great exercise

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:22.960
and you can make walking, more intense too

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:27.960
by speeding up your pace,
or looking to go up hills,

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:31.130
even adding in skipping
and things like that

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:32.420
to make it a little bit more challenging.

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:35.290
So, walking is, I know
it's kind of a go to thing

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:36.580
'cause it's easy to do

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:39.690
and it is very effective,
so walking is great.

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:41.550
You can even throw in other things

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:44.520
with other movements like lunges or squats

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:48.540
and things like that just to
ramp it up a little bit, too.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:51.740
- What do you think about pacing
is it an hour all at once,

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:55.390
or do you imagine it being
three, 20 minute sessions

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:56.740
over the course of the day?

00:10:57.580 --> 00:11:00.050
So, I think breaking it up is the best.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.890
We kind of don't wanna just get our bout

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.250
of physical activity in one time

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:06.160
and then be sedentary the rest of the day.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:08.070
So, one of our recommendations is to,

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:11.440
is getting, using creating a recess time.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.900
I know you all have been talking a lot

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:14.930
and we've all been talking
about the importance

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:16.560
of creating these routines.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:18.640
So again, creating this routine of,

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:21.979
if you know you have lunch
around 12 or 12:30 schedule in

00:11:21.979 --> 00:11:23.990
that 20 to 30 minutes

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:27.990
of dedicated physical
activity time before lunch,

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:29.690
and that's really beneficial

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:33.270
because what it does
to, is before lunch, it.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:35.020
They're getting that energy out they come

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:36.900
and they're ready to eat,
they're gonna be more likely

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:38.580
to eat those vegetables,

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:40.450
and those fruits those healthy foods

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:41.740
that you're putting in front of them

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:45.283
and it also serves as
like a cooldown period.

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:48.300
So, that after lunch if
you're ready to get back

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:51.320
into the learning aspect into
academics they're settled

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.270
and they're focused and ready to learn.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:57.800
That's super helpful and
my sense of it is not only

00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:59.910
is it important for the
physical activity component

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:01.910
but that blood flowing
throughout the whole body

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.820
is actually useful for the learning itself

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:06.560
so that's why it's good
to go back and forth.

